{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>הפליא עצה.</b> A wonder." "<b>תושיה.</b> Wisdom. Rabbi Moses the Kohen says it is from the root יש, and behold, the meaning is that the yield of the earth and the seeds is better than the outcome of their hearing the words of the prophet, which does not help. And the opposite of this is יערף כמטר לקחי (Deuteronomy 32:2), as I explained it."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:55:42.294296043Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}